# Recursive type alias: a type that references itself in field positions.
# Before the fix, recursive positions returned Type::Unknown, silently widening
# the field types. Now they return a fresh TypeVar that can be unified with the
# alias body, giving recursive fields a proper type.
# The type alias itself evaluates to Dict({}) at runtime (a type-level marker).
# The key property verified: type-checking this recursive alias does not
# infinite-loop or error, and evaluation produces correct results.
[
  Node: [type [value: Int next: Node]]
  result: 42
]
=== out
Dict({"result": Int(42)})
